This is important recon. Key facts confirmed about MyDataPlant auth:
- The real backend host is `https://portal.mydataplant.com/api/v3` (NOT suedzuckergroup.com front-end — the doc examples point to the actual API host)
- Auth: JWT-based
- `POST /tokens` — generate token with LOGIN_NAME (email) + PASSWORD, no auth header allowed. This is a password-authenticated login endpoint (username enumeration is out of scope; and this would be brute-force out of scope). 
- JWT payload: `sub`=loginName, `userId`, `email`, `aud: rest-client`, `iss: auth-backend`

