Analysis complete. I fetched the real epp v1.8.0 bundle + lazy chunks and extracted the exact partner-scoping request shapes. Summary of what the JS proves:

- **`x-selected-partner-link-id` header value = server-issued `partnerLinkId`** (from `getExternalAccountPartnerLinks()`), not the predictable 7-digit `partnerNo`. Taken from `withSelectedPartner()` in CxM5FF_V.js. PBOLA-via-guess weakens; the header is set on **only 3 calls**: `POST /external-account/current-partner`, `GET /access-rights`, and impersonation calls.
- **Impersonation surface**: `GET|POST /external-partner-impersonations` (GET with `partnerSearch`, POST `{partnerNo}`), route `/association/impersonation` (middleware `only-for-partner` — client-side). POST is a **state-changing** cross-tenant primitive keyed on partnerNo.
- **`POST /external-account/current-partner?applicationType=EXTERNAL_PLANT_PORTAL`** persists the selected partner server-side — an authorization-state mutation on the Bearer/JWT, giving the backend a per-token "current partner" it could use on later scoped reads.
- New public surface: `GET /api/catalog/companies` returns 200 unauthenticated (SZ/RT/CHILE/SLS/SZP multi-company map). `/rmp/` is ironically the same epp SPA shell — red herring closed.

---

STEP 1 — DELTA
- [NEW] plantportal `/api/catalog/companies` — unauthenticated 200 exposing internal multi-company ID↔code↔name map (SZ=1000, RT=2001, CHILE=2331, SLS=4100, SZP=5000) — new public surface outside the api-gateway
- [NEW] plantportal partner-scoping request family (from D8rUBrrz/CxM5FF_V/Cs2EQOM0/DkCSdWmr): `GET /external-account?applicationType=EXTERNAL_PLANT_PORTAL`, `POST /external-account/current-partner` +header `x-selected-partner-link-id`, `GET /access-rights` +same header, `GET|POST /external-partner-impersonations` (+`partnerSearch`,`{partnerNo}`), `GET/PUT/DELETE /partner-link-processes[/…]`
- [CHANGED] PBOLA confidence down: header value is a **server-issued `partnerLinkId`**, resolved client-side from the user's OWN `/external-account` list — raw 7-digit `partnerNo` never reaches the header
- [CHANGED] `/rmp/` serves the same epp SPA (importmap `#entry`→`/_nuxt/DpUprWo9.js`) — no standalone legacy RMP app; `/rmp/app/common/*` are epp client-side routes
- [NEW] BFF client model (DKcbjuTX): every domain-backend call carries only `Authorization: Bearer` + `x-user-locale`; tenant header is opt-in per-call — backend must enforce partner scope itself

